Benchmark code and data
=======================

No third-party benchmark code or data is bundled with Real2SimLab (the package, this
repository or the published images). Adapters download them at run time, at pinned versions,
into the user's cache, under their own licenses:

- 4DCodeBench (https://github.com/4DCodeBench/4DCodeBench, commit
  6c466be34107d7f388f30f97bf059b68ba1a21b0; Hugging Face datasets 4DCodeBench/Dataset-Synthetic
  and 4DCodeBench/Dataset-Real-World): no license is declared for the code or the data.
  Real2SimLab neither copies nor redistributes them; tasks built from them are marked not
  redistributable. 4DCodeBench's own Docker images are built by each user from its checkout
  and never published by this project.
- IRIS (https://huggingface.co/datasets/rasulkhanbayov/IRIS, revision
  0529a5e0cbbf45d43de2ee1ed7cb98e18de03782): CC-BY-NC-4.0 (non-commercial). Khanbayov,
  Barhdadi, Serpedin, Kurban, "IRIS: A Real-World Benchmark for Inverse Recovery and
  Identification of Physical Dynamic Systems from Monocular Video", ECCV 2026. Downloaded when
  tasks are built, never redistributed.
- PhysCodeGym (https://github.com/ShaoShuai0605/PhysCodeGym, commit
  de1c8b75cddff0054f77b6322a979759e7a01f81): code under the MIT license, run from the user's
  cache; its videos (Hugging Face dataset ShaoShuai0605/PhysCodeGym) keep their sources'
  licenses and are not redistributed.
- Physics-IQ (https://github.com/google-deepmind/physics-IQ-benchmark, commit
  d3f3de16a9c66b4d3bfd6bdb5518570e8b72ad48): code under the Apache License 2.0, run from the
  user's cache; videos under CC-BY-4.0, downloaded from the public Google Cloud Storage bucket
  physics-iq-benchmark (or the Hugging Face dataset Anates-Labs-Research/Physics-IQ-Verified)
  when tasks are built, never redistributed. Motamed, Culp, Swersky, Jaini, Geirhos, "Do
  generative video models understand physical principles?", arXiv:2501.09038.

- Video2World (https://github.com/AetherLabsAI/Video2World, commit
  df0e00b7893b24968e87c5a51a67d824482e431b): code under the Apache License 2.0, run from the
  user's cache. Its dataset (Hugging Face AetherLabs-AI/Video2World, revision
  9cac08429be06ad190b22d6e172af2f815024e3f) adapts samples from other datasets, which keep their
  own terms: DROID (CC-BY-4.0, Khazatsky et al., "DROID: A Large-Scale In-The-Wild Robot
  Manipulation Dataset", 2024), real2sim-eval and PhysTwin (MIT), FurnitureBench (no license
  declared for its data). Downloaded when tasks are built, never redistributed.
- PhySimCode (dataset https://huggingface.co/datasets/SourajaKundu123/PhySimCode, revision
  1d03cd78fe25261af9c1f39d64c5fc438985b8eb): MIT, downloaded when tasks are built, never
  redistributed. Its evaluation code (https://github.com/SourajaKundu/PhySimCode, commit
  e876cd202228b27491ea9e391926246bf15c8749) declares no license: it is fetched from its authors
  when tasks are scored and is not copied or redistributed. Kundu, Gupta, Julin, Zhao, Xie, Jeni,
  "PhySimCode: A Benchmark and Evaluation Method for Physics Video to Code Generation",
  arXiv:2610.15722.

The example recording in examples/raw/puck_slide was rendered by Real2SimLab and is CC0-1.0.

Icons and trademarks
====================

The logo (docs/assets/logo-*.svg) and the projects' symbols (favicon.svg and symbol-*.svg there)
are part of Real2SimLab (Apache-2.0). They come from the logo family of Real2SimHub (assets/brand
in https://github.com/Real2SimHub/Real2SimHub.github.io, with its drawing script); the logo's
lettering is outlined from the fonts Outfit and Chakra Petch (SIL Open Font License 1.1). scripts/make_icons.py writes the icons in docs/assets/icons, also embedded in the
teaser and the social preview:

- Each agent's and benchmark's own icon, as it publishes it, scaled and placed on a tile: the
  project's logo (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, mini-swe-agent, Harbor, Physics-IQ,
  4DCodeBench, PhysCodeGym, PhySimCode) or, without one, its GitHub organization's avatar
  (Codex: OpenAI; Video2World: Aether AI; IRIS: Kurban Intelligence Lab). Claude Code's
  favicon is published only as a small raster, so its tile is redrawn from the vector spark
  in Claude Code's documentation logo, in the favicon's colours.
- The mark of the institution that publishes each of them (a benchmark's first authors'
  institution): the GitHub organization avatars of OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Anomaly, Laude
  Institute, Google DeepMind and Aether AI; Shanghai Jiao Tong University's emblem from its
  visual identity site (vi.sjtu.edu.cn); the seals of Johns Hopkins University and Carnegie
  Mellon University as their brand guidelines publish them (the copies English Wikipedia uses
  as non-free logos); and, from Wikimedia Commons, the Princeton University shield (public
  domain) and the emblem cropped from Hamad Bin Khalifa University's 2016 logo (CC BY-SA 4.0,
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HBKU_Logo,_2016.jpg; the cropped icon,
  docs/assets/icons/org-hbku.svg, is under the same license).
- Generic glyphs for the Lab's own steps and for pipelines: Material Design Icons
  (Pictogrammers, https://pictogrammers.com), Apache-2.0, as bundled with mkdocs-material.

The source URL of every logo is in scripts/make_icons.py. The README's badges are rendered by
shields.io at view time and are not stored here.

These names and logos (OpenAI, Codex, Anthropic, Claude, Claude Code, Google, Gemini, Google
DeepMind, the benchmarks', agents', companies' and universities' names and marks) are
trademarks of their owners. They are used only to identify the software and benchmarks
Real2SimLab runs and who publishes them; no affiliation or endorsement is implied.

Runtime images
==============

`r2s env build` builds, and the project publishes, these images from the Dockerfiles in
docker/. They contain third-party software under its own license:

- r2s-python: Debian 12 (bookworm) packages, including ffmpeg (LGPL/GPL as packaged by
  Debian; source at https://sources.debian.org), Python 3.11 (PSF License), NumPy and SciPy
  (BSD-3-Clause), and the Real2SimLab twin SDK (Apache-2.0).
- r2s-verifier: r2s-python plus pydantic and tomli-w (MIT).
- r2s-agent-codex: r2s-python plus Node.js 22 (MIT) and the OpenAI Codex CLI (Apache-2.0).
- r2s-agent-gemini-cli: r2s-python plus Node.js 22 (MIT) and Gemini CLI (Apache-2.0).
- r2s-agent-opencode: r2s-python plus Node.js 22 (MIT) and OpenCode (MIT).
- r2s-blender-4.0: r2s-python plus Blender 4.0.2 (GPL-2.0-or-later), the official binary
  release from https://download.blender.org/release/Blender4.0/ (its source:
  https://download.blender.org/source/blender-4.0.2.tar.xz). Real2SimLab runs Blender as a
  separate program.

Not published, built by each user:

- r2s-agent-codex-blender: r2s-blender-4.0 plus Node.js 22 (MIT) and the OpenAI Codex CLI
  (Apache-2.0); built locally only because of its size.
- r2s-video2world: r2s-python plus PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), ManiSkill and SAPIEN (Apache-2.0)
  and their dependencies, and ManiSkill assets: ManiSkill-XArm6 (Apache-2.0), the Bridge
  real2sim assets (MIT) and ManiSkill-WidowX250S (no license declared, so this image is never
  published).
- r2s-agent-codex-video2world: r2s-video2world plus Node.js 22 (MIT) and the OpenAI Codex CLI.
- r2s-physimcode: r2s-python plus Matplotlib (PSF-based Matplotlib license).

- r2s-agent-claude-code: r2s-python plus Claude Code, which is proprietary software of
  Anthropic PBC ("All rights reserved"; https://code.claude.com/docs/en/legal-and-compliance).
